 the history then at least  watch it for the babes  [Music]  also one of my favorites Sengoku Basara  samurai kings comes in at number six  from massive battles to powerful  warlords that can destroy entire armies  with a single blow this story highlights  a tale of good versus evil and you may  be thinking well isn't that cliche well  it doesn't seem to be the case for this  anime at first we're presented with many  different characters who fought in  politics and arms with the hopes of  unifying the country under a central  government but eventually they put their  differences aside to fight a common  enemy the demon king of the six heavens  oda nobunaga to save feudal japan from  his tyrannical reign the story is by far  the weakest point of the series however  watching a warrior wielding six swords  with his two hands can be quite  entertaining almost like watching Zorro  from one piece working his craft halfway  to the top now and in at number five we  have the record of Grand Crest war the  joyful marriage ceremony that would  establish peace between two power blocks  eventually turns out into tragedy with  the release of chaos chaos is a dark  energy from another dimension which  brings forth monsters and demons into  the world only the lords with the power  of crests can stock chaos but they  allowed greed and pride to defeat their  common purpose and instead of fighting a  collective battle to stop chaos the  Lords fight each other for the power of  crests having witnessed the disaster  firsthand our hero in mage meets a young  warrior named Theo who is also carrying  a mysterious crest together they'll  fight battle after battle and tried to  restore balance to their war-torn land  so if you're looking for a combat  oriented adventurer with plenty of  in-depth strategizing in massive battles  and just a little touch of romance we'll  definitely find this show very  entertaining  [Music]  at number 4 is Bhutan where Oh moon oh  god that's not an easy title 