hing  during their escapades our main man guts  proves to be a mighty addition to  Griffiths force together they'll fight  and win many battles and just when you  think the world starts looking better  for guts the world ends up crumbling  around him as the series spirals further  into a far darker realm of fantasy  horror that could force some people to  stop watching altogether and by the way  make sure you watch the older version if  you're new to anime because there's a  new 3d version and basically don't  bother with that  we've got just one step left before we  get to the summit but to number two we  have Kingdom okay before I start this  one I've got it advise you not to lose  interest because of the poor 3d  animation in the first episodes of this  series because to be frank I did but  thankfully I had both the willpower and  the patience to carry on once you get  past the bad quality of the initial  episodes it becomes a smooth sail season  2 &amp; 3 a much better and visual quality  and with that said let's get to the  story in the era of the warring kingdoms  China was fragmented into seven powerful  states with each trying to conquer the  other the story follows an orphaned  child named Shin shin and his best  friend both have the dream of becoming  great generals but they had no idea what  fate had in store for them they soon end  up getting separated with shins friend  getting enlisted to work in the royal  palace by a retainer of the king shin on  the other hand has to face some serious  problems including finding his friend  half dead at his doorstep he sets out to  find out who did it and why they did it  a mission that would drastically change  shins life Kingdom demonstrates some  incredibly large scale military fights  and for the most part the series did an  excellent job capturing the feel and  realities of the battlefield the manga  is one of the best-selling manga out  there so if you're not able to tolerate  the first episodes with bad animation  then try reading the manga I think this  must be the first time I've ever said  try reading the manga  nah  ring the bell and sound the alarm for  our number one entry today is the  Vinland saga at the start of the 11th  century Europe suffers from the  incessant raids of the Viking tribes the  war between England and the Danes  getting worse with each passing year  after witnessing the murder of his  father tor Finn sets out to take revenge  on the killer however his chances are  quite slim considering his young age so  he makes a long-term plan by joining the  army of his enemy this made him stronger  while plotting his revenge and preparing  himself with a perfect moment to strike  Aska lad in turn uses tor fiends  irresistible impulse to his advantage  he's entrusted him with the most  dangerous tasks with his mercenary band  of Vikings they burned villages kill  people and loot to their delight it's an  interesting story with realistic  characters in a violent yet beautifully  captured world which is brought to life  by rich colors beautiful animations and  great fights and that's it for today's  episode of the top ten list do you  believe there are some anime series that  should have made the list let me know by  leaving a comment below thanks for  watching be sure to share like and  subscribe to our Channel
 

